  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Change of use of the dwelling (C3) to a children's care home (C2) for up to two children aged 7-18",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&nbsp;The proposed development would result&nbsp;in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the Development Plan and supporting evidence base. Furthermore, the applicant fails to accurately demonstrate that there&nbsp;is an identified need for the children&#39;s home and the type of care proposed,&nbsp;which&nbsp;would not meet the current needs of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham (LBBD) Children’s Social Care, as confirmed by&nbsp;LBBD&#39;s Lead Commissioner in Children&#39;s Social Care. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s supply of family housing, would fail to meet local need and is therefore contrary to the following policies:&nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024) Policy&nbsp;D7, H1, H12 and S2 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP3 and&nbsp;SPDG1 of the LBBD Local Plan&nbsp; (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development lacks information and therefore clarity associated with the number of children who would be cared for in the home.&nbsp;The proposal could prejudice third parties who may otherwise have wished to comment on the application; the proposed development cannot be accurately assessed with regards to quality of accommodation and impact to neighbours and thus it cannot be demonstrated that it would be supported by the Development Plan.&nbsp;As such, the proposal is contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD1 of&nbsp;&nbsp;the LBBD Local Plan&nbsp; (September 2024)"
  ],
